5:> Detailed runs and issue evidence remain in the external smoke harness cataloged by `project-index.md`.
7:Deep smoke runs after sprint review. It is not a substitute for unit tests or `review.md`; it proves runtime-facing claims with executable evidence and links the relevant external harness run and issue records. Every normal smoke run first uses the configured smoke author model to inspect the sprint and target, create or update a durable sprint-specific suite in the external harness, and declare exactly which non-deterministic coverage that suite owns. UltraPlan then discovers and executes that authored suite.
9:Normal smoke execution must not change product source, product tests, governed sprint inputs, product documentation, or Git state. It may change only manifest-declared harness authoring paths, harness-declared run/evidence paths, sprint smoke flow state, and sprint-root `smoke.md`. UltraPlan records the author run and changed harness paths and rejects out-of-scope mutations.
21:Resolve the target, harness root, versioned harness manifest, `runs/`, and `issues/` from `project-index.md`. Read the governed sprint inputs, execute evidence, current `review.md`, and flow state. Review must be current and `pass`/`pass_with_findings` by default; failed/stale review requires an explicit diagnostic override.
25:Run the configured smoke author against the governed requirements, reasoning, plan, execute evidence, review, product target, existing deterministic tests, and current harness. Build a coverage matrix for behaviors that normal unit and integration tests do not prove deterministically: real provider/model calls when the product path uses them, actual process and signal behavior, real filesystem/configuration boundaries, real network services, real browser engines, credentials, timing, cancellation, and platform behavior.
29:## 3. Read The Machine Harness Contract
